<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:27Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is Germany's eight-hour workday under threat?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1793a7a470b7815adacdca42f5b7dd313a5a1b93a11e90421de951b28c39e2b1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984--28b0ad264d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Would you work 12 hours straight? The CDU/CSU and SPD are locked in a dispute over reforms to the Working Hours Act. Workplace flexibility, collective bargaining agreements and worker protection rules are at stake.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>France reports more than 1,800 arrests after riots, looting and arson during cost-of-living protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df71fb5ed5850001b346d3ea4787505965c817c7f6d14ef59e6294c937e94747</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-reports-more-than-1-800-arrests-after-riots-looting-and-arson-during-cost-of-living-protests/a-79692322--728def49fc88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-reports-more-than-1-800-arrests-after-riots-looting-and-arson-during-cost-of-living-protests/a-79692322?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rioters torched public buildings and looted shops across France, destroying Limoges' historic town hall. The violence erupted during nationwide cost-of-living protests.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Vietnam signs free trade deal with four European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cca1df868fa6e97670a27abde04d18cbba75db70b0ad1648dd4effc8fbc4088a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812--7e41481b6a6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has signed a deal with four non-EU members that covers trade in goods and services, intellectual property rights, and sustainable development, among other areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How reliant is Ukraine on the US-controlled Starlink internet service?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fd7045fa872cbed4cf65fdb3afde147e69d871e61af0e7d676b86df8a34d970</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729--6217d664b01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kyiv keeps issuing warnings that the satellite internet system Starlink is being restricted in Ukraine. How dependent is the country on the system, and what would happen if it went down?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police probe security incident at Leipzig/Halle airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d278e5905033946203284054b5fc72acb413fcdd4e3888c85374d4de9a547b69</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913--f152414b1a9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fence breach at the Leipzig/Halle airport has triggered a major police operation. Christian Social Union leader Markus Söder is to address a gathering of the conservative youth wing. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Populist Czech PM Babis goes empty-handed in Senate elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4dd5e59bb96369f8a7fe96ebf7840c4a11270de8b9eae07165ca6e8fbb18432</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934--95037aa1aa28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties still control the Czech Senate, in a major blow to Prime Minister Andrej Babis' and his governing coalition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke released after detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f742fc2bb4cc34b6128a1e5c0ed6d304c1a49579830425872a2fd0116b7c9ac4</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933--80500fd3a662.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two other prominent CJP leaders are set to be released on Sunday. India has seen huge rallies calling on the country's top election official to step down over alleged manipulation of voter rolls.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata stampede dampens Durga Puja festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40641d09edada5268a1819c8d69b6b3d03cd80f510fa2c4493335dcf902dd661</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T04:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143--9e78a7d0cccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have detained several people over a deadly stampede in India's eastern city of Kolkata, after the state vowed strict action. Meanwhile, 'Cockroach' leader Dipke is out of detention. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Major fire reported at military base in Alberta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76cf6ded28bf38ddaa0dfef34fa2270b91d3859a5e9cbe8252b0474166271dce</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T02:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-major-fire-reported-at-military-base-in-alberta/a-79690515--194f6f97e468.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-major-fire-reported-at-military-base-in-alberta/a-79690515?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney has said a "serious incident" sparked a major fire at a military base in Alberta. He did not provide details on the cause of the fire.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'No Kings' rallies push early voting ahead of US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8596f0b23d651e76b0510c8ae24ab4cad212391849db896e4fb5671dde57308</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T00:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-kings-rallies-push-early-voting-ahead-of-us-midterm-elections/a-79690502--c2c75c7f5f7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-kings-rallies-push-early-voting-ahead-of-us-midterm-elections/a-79690502?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Organizers of the "No Kings" protests, known for their anti-Trump sentiment, are urging Americans to vote early in the November 3 midterm elections, as Republicans face tough races to retain control of Congress.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ilhan Omar: The US Democrat targeted by Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f73dc3f27ed854dd59f67859a89024d347396cbc5cdfa5fd49c9f2ed8750bc3</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T19:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ilhan-omar-the-us-democrat-targeted-by-donald-trump/a-79688445--0b2fbb5ba398.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ilhan-omar-the-us-democrat-targeted-by-donald-trump/a-79688445?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has described her as "garbage" and a "criminal" who does nothing but "bitch." Congress member Ilhan Omar has long been the target of angry verbal attacks from the US president. But why her?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Romanian fighter jets shoot down 2 drones over Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edd901cdfe08922ad369d45d44242af0152098337c355ab1b40bb1a104247a9d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romanian-fighter-jets-shoot-down-2-drones-over-black-sea/a-79689156--bd62b985e5d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romanian-fighter-jets-shoot-down-2-drones-over-black-sea/a-79689156?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Romanian Air Force F-16s shot down drones over Romanian territorial waters. Earlier this week, two chemical tankers were hit by drones near Romania's Black Sea coast.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt's Ssisi says he'll defend Saudi Arabia, if asked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c12e6414b0238a0e498e74a75a07c0c4563bbdc07d31afd3fdd2e519f3f68579</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-s-ssisi-says-he-ll-defend-saudi-arabia-if-asked/a-79689105--a11b59189924.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-s-ssisi-says-he-ll-defend-saudi-arabia-if-asked/a-79689105?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Egyptian president said his country was ready to defend Saudi Arabia "if requested." The comments come amid escalating Houthi attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Israeli settlers attack EU diplomats, French mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24a10d3d431c6ba48d4f170a1f94e0d37c195dc60934508db09fd98140a2f7b1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settlers-attack-eu-diplomats-french-mayor/a-79688819--13df4c5f717b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settlers-attack-eu-diplomats-french-mayor/a-79688819?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A group of Israeli settlers attacked vehicles carrying European diplomats in the West Bank, a day after an American photographer was beaten. Belgium and France have condemned the attack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:662b32d8ba39f834f0bb4c5637c746b96988aaeb1cd6b41a4397d7ee76695f3a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dde3abb0b99299d2b1d2a9387714d3581718379939af01081fa8b67aa7bc3b65</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo leaves hospital after cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f6c4b63a7875d310aa64e20184cd38de47c45773ab47774ea44ad651d6da198</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162--69f6144ccc39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Four days after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Leo left the hospital in Rome. His doctors said he was well enough to return home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9837fddcec3480be92e0ee267a42eee6a05d4cefeefc79fc1b9aa32c63841c1a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703--c66cb23b1a91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy says Russia is trying to cut electricity and heating to civilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico sentences killers of US, Australian surfers to 158 years each in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:854c9c05a8e0a321ab5a6ec3c429905b2959848e189253b3e4c7a524b6addc42</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975--d9f256fde01a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three Mexican men were found guilty last week of murdering foreign surfers in 2024. The case had drawn global condemnation, particularly in Australia, where two of the victims were from.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Protesters clash with police in nationwide protests, amid rising social polarization</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4e63a6dd397081688b0848dec144dce02d807f619c1cbc6b873d8b9a3503907</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584--b410e6f9b726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Unrest broke out in parts of France as students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists took to the streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police arrested over 1,000 people amid chaotic scenes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: California wildfires destroy homes, leave thousands without power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed2dc29f67bbbe31605dca5174b3620f1a1e636ec194f0f38346babcc673163a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480--49bdc655ff84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Multiple mansions have been engulfed in the fires raging in California while firefighters continue to douse the blaze. Thousands of people have been evacuated and many others are without power.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
